I sit at my desk at the office.
I am completely focusing on my computer screen.
Suddenly Peter and Eva are standing behind me.
Eva is carrying a small plate with a piece of pastry.
There is a single lit candle in it.
"Congratulations, Maya!" they say in unison.
I smile broadly because I am very surprised.
"Thank you so much, that is really nice of you," I say.
Peter points at the delicious pastry.
"We bought it at the bakery on the corner this morning," he explains.
"You have worked incredibly hard on our latest project," Eva adds.
"Yes, we finished the project yesterday," Peter says.
"So you have earned a good break now," Eva says and smiles.
I blow out the candle, and my two colleagues clap.
The pastry tastes fantastic with marzipan and chocolate.
We eat it together and drink a cup of coffee.
I have missed Mexico today, but I do not feel alone.
I have found some amazing friends here at the office.
